  "question": {
    "text": "Three rods made of the same material and having the same cross-section are joined as shown in the figure. Each rod is of the same length. What is the temperature at the junction of the three rods (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>)?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0034219_Questiona..jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 218px; height: 143px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "60",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the temperature of function be <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math>, then<br /><br /><math><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo></math> <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-08-27_at_2.54.59_PM.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 147px;\" /><br /><br />Or <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math><br /><br />Or <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math><br /><br />Or <math><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math><br /><br />Or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">℃</mi></math>",
